Amazon Linux's "SnapSafe" patch for OpenSSL, as applied to its openssl-snapsafe-libs package
(source RPM openssl-3.5.8-1.amzn2023.0.3, file 0500-snapsafe-provider.patch, Apache-2.0).
It reseeds OpenSSL's random generator when the generation counter of /dev/sysgenid changes,
i.e. when Lambda SnapStart restores an execution environment from a snapshot.
Applies cleanly to upstream OpenSSL 3.5.8.

